=== Motivation ===

BIP 460 adds one additional output script format: witness version 2 outputs, whose key path spends can participate in cross-input signature aggregation.
The <tt>raw()</tt> and <tt>addr()</tt> descriptors of [[bip-0385.mediawiki|BIP 385]] can represent such an output, but not the keys, derivation paths, and script tree it was built from.
This expression allows specifying that information as a descriptor, so wallets can generate addresses, detect received coins, and back up the spending conditions of witness version 2 outputs.
<tt>tr()</tt> descriptors produce witness version 1 output scripts and therefore cannot describe these outputs.
<tt>rawcisa()</tt> also describes an output known only by its 32-byte output key, for example when the wallet does not know the script tree.

== Specification ==

Two new script expressions are defined: <tt>cisa()</tt> and <tt>rawcisa()</tt>.
The <tt>cisa(KEY)</tt> and <tt>cisa(KEY, TREE)</tt> expressions are specified exactly as <tt>tr(KEY)</tt> and <tt>tr(KEY, TREE)</tt> in BIP 386, including the Tree Expression and the key expression rules, except for the differences in this section.

The <tt>rawcisa(KEY)</tt> expression can only be used as a top level expression.
It takes a single key expression, subject to the same key expression rules as <tt>cisa()</tt>, and uses the resulting 32-byte x-only public key directly as the output key, without the tweak of [[bip-0341.mediawiki|BIP 341]].

=== Output script and address ===

The witness version of the output script is 2 instead of 1:

<pre>
scriptPubKey:       OP_2 <32_byte_output_key>
</pre>

The output scripts are encoded as Bech32m addresses with witness version 2 as specified in [[bip-0350.mediawiki|BIP 350]].

=== Expressions within <tt>cisa()</tt> and <tt>rawcisa()</tt> ===

Other BIPs restrict where their expressions may appear.
[[bip-0387.mediawiki|BIP 387]] allows <tt>multi_a()</tt> and <tt>sortedmulti_a()</tt> only within <tt>tr()</tt>, [[bip-0379.md|BIP 379]] allows Miniscript within <tt>wsh()</tt> and <tt>tr()</tt>, and [[bip-0390.mediawiki|BIP 390]] allows <tt>musig()</tt> within <tt>tr()</tt>, <tt>rawtr()</tt>, and <tt>sp()</tt>.
Any expression that is allowed within a <tt>tr()</tt> descriptor is also allowed in the same position within a <tt>cisa()</tt> descriptor.
Likewise, any expression that is allowed within a <tt>rawtr()</tt> descriptor is also allowed within a <tt>rawcisa()</tt> descriptor.

