== Backward compatibility ==

<tt>cisa()</tt> and <tt>rawcisa()</tt> descriptors use the format and general operation specified in [[bip-0380.mediawiki|BIP 380]].
As these are a set of wholly new descriptors, they are not compatible with any implementation.
The scripts produced are witness version 2 output scripts, see the Backward compatibility section of BIP 460 for how software without witness version 2 support treats them.

== Rationale ==

=== Why a new script expression? ===

A witness version 2 output is a different output type with different spending rules.
Descriptors identify the output type by the script expression, as the pair <tt>pkh()</tt> and <tt>wpkh()</tt> shows, so a new expression follows this convention while a parameter of <tt>tr()</tt> would not.
It also lets implementations without support for BIP 460 reject the descriptor when parsing it instead of silently producing an output they cannot spend.

=== Why no aggregation mode? ===

BIP 460 makes aggregation a per-input decision at signing time, and the output script is the same for all modes.
The mode therefore belongs to the signing process and not to the descriptor.

=== Why <tt>rawcisa()</tt>? ===

Without <tt>rawcisa()</tt>, a witness version 2 output with an unknown script tree could only be described as an unsolvable <tt>addr()</tt>.
An output known only by its output key could not be described at all.
The corresponding <tt>rawtr()</tt> expression is implemented in Bitcoin Core and used by [[bip-0337.mediawiki|BIP 337]], [[bip-0352.mediawiki|BIP 352]], BIP 390, and [[bip-0451.md|BIP 451]], but it is not specified in BIP 386 or any other BIP.
<tt>rawcisa()</tt> therefore cannot be specified by reference and this document defines it in full.

